Ramfication in pre-image towers
There exists a finite set of primes $S$ such that all $K_n$ are unramified outside of $S$. (Known for $\mathbb{P}^1$). \begin{enumerate} \item If not PCF and $X=\mathbb{P}^1$ let $S_n = \{\text{primes of $K$ where $K_n/K$ is ramified}\}$. Is the growth rate of $\#S_n$ related to some height of $f$, specifically $\hat{h}_{crit}$? \item Assume conjecture ($X= \mathbb{P}^1$). Can you arrange it so that all of the ramification in the tower is tame? (even for one example). \end{enumerate}
Let $X$ be a projective variety, $f:X/K \to X/K$ PCF. Let $\alpha \in X(K)$. Look at the tower of fields from adding the pull-backs of $\alpha$ \begin{equation*} K_n = K(f^{-n}(\alpha)). \end{equation*}
Galois Problems
Postcritically finite maps in complex and arithmetic dynamics
A PCF preimage-field tower is unramified outside one finite set of primes.
